This was a scratch “dynamics” layer: if-then spines for how a fight should play
out. It does not fit the model.

Battles are tracked in core states (SE · AP · B/SB·CB · RC · ST). What a fleet
wants is mission × picture × desire. What moves the graph is a transition
tactic. Outcome is the collision of two desires plus track/geometry — not a
predicted path.

This file conflates those: it writes one side’s hoped sequence as if it were
the state machine, ignores the foe’s seat, and treats Cover vs Exit / Approach
commits as extra dynamics instead of tactics. Kept only as a discarded sketch.

