battle dynamics

The battles are primarily tracked in *states* (Search-Approach-Battle-Contact-Strike) not dynamics.  Dynamics is instead the meta layer of how things should be expected to play out given the stances that ships and fleets will behave.  Here is a non exhaustive brainstorming list of expectations for what fleets will want (not necessarily what will happen), expressed in psuedocode:

if (Near_parity or advantage) and not obvious_alternative: search->approach->battle_slugging->battle_slugging (i.e. remain there until change)
if strike_advantage and escape_feasible and not pinned: no_obvious_advantage = false
if strike_advantage and escape_feasible and not pinned: battle->contact->search/strike->strike
if (defending_convoy or defending_station) and not cutting_losses:  pinned = true
if (defending_convoy and (cutting_losses or no_wounded_transports)) and not overwhelming_advantage: battle-> contact -> search -> end_battle
if defending_station and station_can_tank and strike_advantage: battle->contact->strike
if defending_station and strike_disadvantage and not (station_can_tank and waiting_out_strike): strike/battle -> contact -> battle
if poor_coordination and (near_parity or advantage): obvious_alternative = True; search->approach->battle_chaos 
if loss_insensitive_swarm -> search->approach->battle_chaos
if (near_parity or disadvantage) and taking_more_damage and ((not pinned) or cutting_losses): battle->contact->search->end_battle
